// Regression: a BEAM must be RESERVED in the inter-staff gap at the geometry it is DRAWN
// with, not with the fixed DefaultStemLength 3.5 that SkylineBuilder.AddNoteBoxToSkylines
// gives an unbeamed stem. LilyPond's Beam is an ordinary inside-staff grob (no
// outside-staff-priority), so it joins the staff's vertical skyline like the slur and the
// tuplet bracket, and the staff below must clear its outer edge.
//
// Before the seed the corpus saw it nowhere: SkylineBuilder reserved every beamed member's
// stem at 3.5, over-reserving the shortened same-pitch beam. It now suppresses those stems
// (BeamedItemsToSuppress) and seeds the drawn beam's outer edge (AddBeamsToSkyline), from a
// staff-frame BeamLayout (MultiStaffLayouter.StaffBeamLayouts).
//
// The shape is the corpus books BMD/BMU (audit/lp-geometry/probes/page-vertical.ly), which
// pin the same geometry against real LilyPond: staff.staff.beam-{under,over}-notes. The
// pitch puts the noteheads UNDER StaffGrouper's basic-distance of 9 while the down-beam
// beats it, so the gap reads the beam and not the floor. Two voices are required because a
// beam group's direction cannot be forced from a single-note token; the second voice's stems
// (and beam) point down, and voice one holds the middle line.
octave absolute
time 4/4
key c major
title "A beam reserves its room in the staff gap"
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }
section S {
  rh { voice { b1 } voice { g,8 g, g, g, g, g, g, g, } | }
  lh { d,1 | }
}
form main { S }
score main "beam-under-staves" { grandStaff { staff rh staff lh } }
